{"jyesWa": [{"id": "jyezWa", "headword": "ज्येष्ठ", "headword_slp1": "jyezWa", "fold": "jyesWa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Jyeṣṭha, ordinarily meaning ‘greatest,’ has further the specific sense of ‘eldest’ brother in the Rigveda. It also means the eldest among sons, which is another side of the same sense.\nFoot notes With changed accent, jyeṣṭhá. Cf. Macdonell, Vedic Grammar, p. 83, 14.\niv. 33, 5; x. 11, 2.\nAv. xii. 2, 35; aitareya brāhmaṇa, vii. 17; Śatapatha brāhmaṇa, xi. 5, 3, 8, and cf. Jyaiṣthineya.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["jyeShTha", "jyeṣṭha", "జ్యేష్ఠ", "ಜ್ಯೇಷ್ಠ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["jyeShTha", "jyeṣṭha", "జ్యేష్ఠ", "ಜ್ಯೇಷ್ಠ"]}, {"id": "jyezWA", "headword": "ज्येष्ठा", "headword_slp1": "jyezWA", "fold": "jyesWa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Jyeṣṭhā. See nakṣatra.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["jyeShThaa", "jyeṣṭhā", "జ్యేష్ఠా", "ಜ್ಯೇಷ್ಠಾ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["jyeShThaa", "jyeṣṭhā", "జ్యేష్ఠా", "ಜ್ಯೇಷ್ಠಾ"]}], "jyesWa-Gni": [{"id": "jyezWa-GnI", "headword": "ज्येष्ठ-घ्नी", "headword_slp1": "jyezWa-GnI", "fold": "jyesWa-Gni", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Jyeṣṭha-ghnī, ‘slaying the eldest,’ is the name of a nakṣatra, or lunar mansion, usually called jyeṣṭhā, in the Atharvaveda and the taittirīya brāhmaṇa. It is Antares or Cor Scipionis.\nFoot notes vi. 110, 2. Cf. vi. 112, 1.\ni. 5, 2, 8. Cf. Whitney, Translation of the Atharvaveda, 361.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["ghnee", "ghni", "ghnii", "ghnī", "jyeShTha", "jyeShTha-ghnee", "jyeShTha-ghni", "jyeShTha-ghnii", "jyeShThaghnee", "jyeShThaghni", "jyeShThaghnii", "jyeṣṭha", "jyeṣṭha-ghni", "jyeṣṭha-ghnī", "jyeṣṭhaghni", "jyeṣṭhaghnī", "घ्नि", "घ्नी", "ज्येष्ठ", "ज्येष्ठ-घ्नि", "ज्येष्ठघ्नि", "ज्येष्ठघ्नी", "ఘ్ని", "ఘ్నీ", "జ్యేష్ఠ", "జ్యేష్ఠ-ఘ్ని", "జ్యేష్ఠ-ఘ్నీ", "జ్యేష్ఠఘ్ని", "జ్యేష్ఠ